CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Unknown "This flag the reason for the internal interlock is unknown";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Reboot "This flag is set if a reboot tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Voltage_DC "This flag is set if a voltage on DC tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_W_Low "This flag is set if a low current on W tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_W_High "This flag is set if a hight current on W tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_V_Low "This flag is set if a low current on V tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_V_High "This flag is set if a hight current on V tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_U_Low "This flag is set if a low current on U tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ SG_ 2147975254 Current_U_High "This flag is set if a hight current on U tripped the internal interlock";
CM_ BO_ 2147942481 " This message is used to define the droop characteristics of the module in Inverter 3-Phase operation. The droop curve for both voltage and frequency is 
              defined as a symetric 3 linear segments. The 'nominal' segment is defined solely
              by the slope (it intersects the zero). Then the other two segments, called
              'auxiliary' are symetric around the zero, and they are defined by an intersection 
              point and another slope. For more info, check the user manual.
      ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Enable_Legacy_Mode " If legacy mode is enabled, module will behave as previous to the
                introduction of the droop feature. It will generate the AC waveform in 
                open loop, and will not be able to be paralleled.
        ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Enable_Integral_Action " Enable integral action for the Power loops. Enable this only if connected
                to the utility grid. If you go off-grid, this bit must be immediately cleared.
                This is disabled by default on startup.";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Disable_Harmonic_Compensation " Set this flag when harmonic compensation needs to be disabled (i.e, when 
                the module is connected in parallel to the grid or to other diesel generators).
                Harmonic compensation is enabled by default on startup. ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Virtual_Impedance " Sets the inductive virtual impedance in microhenries (uH). By default
                    (i.e: after power cycle), this value is 8000 uH";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Volt_droop_nominal " Sets the nominal droop slope for the Voltage in V/MegaWatt. By default
                    (i.e: after power cycle), this value is 648 V/MW";
CM_ SG_ 2147942481 Freq_droop_nominal " Sets the nominal droop slope for the Frequency in Hz/MegaWatt. By default
                    (i.e: after power cycle), this value is 40 Hz/MW ";
CM_ BO_ 2147942478 "Control of the setpoints in DC/DC modes (buck and boost)";
CM_ SG_ 2147942478 negative_current_limit "The current limit in reverse direction. (Phases->DC in Buck, DC->Phases in Boost) This limit applies to the phase side currents";
CM_ SG_ 2147942478 positive_current_limit "The current limit for current in forward direction (DC->Phases in Buck, Phases->DC in Boost), this limit applies to the phase side currents";
CM_ SG_ 2147942478 Voltage_Setpoint "The voltage setpoint in DC/DC modes. This message is an alternate way of defining the 'normal' voltage setpoint, but only applies in DC/DC modes. In boost mode this value needs to be larger than the low side voltage at all times.";
CM_ BO_ 2147942477 "Set parameters for DC Droop control";
CM_ SG_ 2147942477 Droop_resistance_negative_curren "Virtual droop resistance in Ohms when current is negative. Its default 
                value after power cycling is 1 Ohm for VA08,VA01 and VA04 variants, and 3 Ohm for VA03
                variant.";
CM_ SG_ 2147942477 Droop_resistance_positive_curren "Virtual droop resistance in Ohms when current is positive. Its default
              value after power cycling is 1 Ohm for VA08,VA01 and VA04 variants, and 3 Ohm for VA03
              variant.";
CM_ SG_ 2147942477 Enable "Flag to enable droop. If enabled, the voltage Setpoint
          will be modified according to the following equation:
          Vref' = Vref - I*Rdroop. Droop is disabled by default upon
          power cycle.";
CM_ BO_ 2147942513 "The setpoints that apply to the AFE in Rectifier Mode.
            The rectifier mode operates a CV/CC control of the DC bus side,
            with the Currents on the AC following the needs of the DC bus.
            With the Real power defined by the needs of the AC bus the AFE may
            still provide inductive or capacitive reactive power.
      ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942513 DC_Sink_current_limit " The maximum current that BP25 will draw from the DC Bus.
                If the measured DC bus voltage is above the target voltage the BP25 will draw
                current from the DC bus in order to lower the voltage. This signal limits the
                maximum current the BP25 may draw from the bus. If this current is reached
                the Voltage of the Bus is no longer controlled by the BP25, as it now operates in
                constant current mode (CC)
        ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942513 DC_Source_current_limit "The maximum current that the BP25 will provide to the DC Bus.
              If the measured voltage is below the target voltage the BP25 will provide
              current to the DC bus in order to raise it's voltage. This signal limits the
                maximum current the BP25 may provide to the bus. If this current is reached
                the Voltage of the Bus is no longer controlled by the BP25, as it now operates in
                constant current mode (CC)
        ";
CM_ SG_ 2147942513 DC_Bus_Voltage_setpoint "The voltage that the rectifier targets on the DC bus.";
CM_ BO_ 2147975282 "The currently applied setpoints for the setpoints configured in AFE_Rectifier_Setpoints.
            For details please see the signal descriptions in 'AFE_Rectifier_Setpoints'
      ";
CM_ BO_ 2147975248 " Reads the droop resistance values of user ";
